-- title:
--   ̄ j(q^ℓ) lies outside the Igusa function field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\kappa$ a field of characteristic $p$, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.IntegralWeightOneForm`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L16): a modular form `w.form` of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$, together with a power series `w.series` over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the weight-one $q$-expansion of `w.form`, and subject to the requirement that the reduction `intSeriesC κ w.series` — the image of `w.series` in $\kappa[[q]] \subseteq \kappa((q))$ — be nonzero. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ne p$ and $\ell \nmid M$. The assertion is that the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC κ ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), obtained from the reduction mod $p$ of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image of `jNum` in $\kappa[[q]]$, by the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$, is not an element of [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C κ M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))/\kappa$ generated by the underlying set of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC κ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) $=$ `qExpFunctionFieldC κ (Gamma1 M)` together with the single element $($`intSeriesC κ w.series`$)^{-1}$. (The instance $\ell \ne 0$ needed to form the substitution is supplied from the primality of $\ell$.)
--
--   This is the non-membership half of the computation of the degree of $\bar j(q^{\ell})$ over the Igusa function field of level $M$ in characteristic $p$: the Igusa field is an abelian (Kummer) layer over the function field of $X_1(M)$, whereas adjoining $\bar j(q^{\ell})$ for $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \ne p$ produces a non-normal extension of degree $\ell+1$. It feeds the degree statement [`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqNModC_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq), the hypotheses $\ell \ne p$ and $\ell \nmid M$ being both necessary, since $\bar j(q^{p}) = \bar j^{\,p}$ and $\bar j(q^{\ell})$ already lies in the level-$M$ field when $\ell \mid M$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_jqNModC_not_mem_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_of_not_dvd.lean

